 the following could be the graph of a function $f(x)$ that satisfies the conditions below?\n\n- ${f}^{′}(x)>0$, for all $x\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )$\n\n- $f(2)=2.$" :question/worked-solution "We summarize all the given information in the following table: \n\n| $x$ | $(-\\infty ,2)$ | $2$ | $(2,\\infty )$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}^{′}$ | $+$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n| $f$ |  | $2$ |  |\n\nThis gives us the following information about the graph of $f:$\n\n| $x$ | $(-\\infty ,2)$ | $2$ | $(2,\\infty )$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}^{′}$ | $+$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n| $f$ | $↗$ | $2$ | $↗$ |\n\nSo, we can conclude that\n\n- the graph of $y=f(x)$ must pass through the point $(2,2),$ and\n\n- $f(x)$ is increasing on $(-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each graph:\n\n|  | I | II | III | IV | V |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Passes through $(2,2)$ | $✓$ | $✓$ | $✓$ | $✓$ | $✓$ |\n| $↗$ on $(-\\infty ,\\infty )$ | $\\times $ | $✓$ | $\\times $ | $\\times $ | $\\times $ |\n\nTherefore, a possible graph of $f$ is as follows:  \n\n![](images/5d/5d725bd68f0278e429a0aa2ab2d4a78942b75d6e5095c2d01158ae7dbd3cca9a.png)"} :step/id #uuid "0b6d7cce-d70b-50be-8b0e-be43d18ea6f9" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186507591}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186507558 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186507485 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "33726455-c820-556e-8b6f-a4d63e8d5a14" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/bc/bc94ac2bc9270ee681022a7578b95802342456fe0d82bb6cedf478ed3260d18a.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506802} {:answer/id #uuid "4942f91f-eba9-5b4f-8a10-d9a7e4ccf0f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/47/47c6b7b69c4f76680f0e32ddf886af3d0b440ccc773427be69d7b2271c979cf5.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506851} {:answer/id #uuid "58648f90-1e35-5210-bd96-6ffd2ad1b4f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/df/df8dc281941de401464bf5a7ca9