Therefore, a possible graph of $f$ could be as follows: \n\n![](images/35/35e5a713c8649bee4fb1a03f44a87feef082d9046168d8d0486b161c530327dc.png)"} :step/id #uuid "753f4d28-3233-572d-b81f-1283afa4468f"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186507583 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186507509 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "41253b36-5553-5597-b245-69b33e4b54b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/10/100c82d259cc058f3cd12eafe5a40e6118f613acf501883173b9d065b2c58841.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506830} {:answer/id #uuid "7870bd0f-18db-56b8-a7f7-47125fc4b860" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/cb/cb4eb2f229282853c74ea660f1054ae846b22acb0de0e946b377f53aff48f0ca.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506947} {:answer/id #uuid "807860fa-8148-5eb8-a5a0-6b810fde6ffb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/c6/c66525cd280864b95baa312bfce24b206a099add3d1de87d99e59137a20d734c.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506962} {:answer/id #uuid "a5f1ba1d-f867-5cde-855c-2d4a288b7c0e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/30/30f1172b43bbcef9b86afc7c61af24d9e43eb38041db8b4c5db28287c2ce3d8d.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507040} {:answer/id #uuid "f0f3e65f-33d0-5369-9188-196509b1c9ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/e2/e243e12effdf4f61a210e42fbda7aad253c091777d4f247c6b330a5dafd15506.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507210}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186506830} :answer-field/id #uuid "03b77cad-c238-5633-b063-acdffbafe9f4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507243}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "d6e3cdba-2429-5682-a282-855cddfb8eeb" :question/math-academy-id "q-117073" :question/problem "Which of the following could be the graph of a continuous function $f(x)$ that satisfies the conditions below?\n\n- ${f}^{′}(x)$ and ${f}^{″}(x)$ are undefined at $x=1$\n\n- if $x\\in (-\\infty ,1)$ then ${f}^{′}(x)>0$ and if $x\\in (1,\\infty )$ then ${f}^{′}(x)<0$\n\n- ${f}^{″}(x)>0$ for all $x\\in (-\\infty ,1)\\cup (1,\\infty )$" :question/worked-solution "We summarize all the given information in the following table:\n\n| $x$ | $(-\\infty ,1)$ | $1$ | $(1,\\infty )$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}^{′}$ | $+$ | $\\text{undef.}$ | $-$ |\n| ${f}^{″}$ | $+$ | $\\text{undef.}$ | $+$ |\n| $f$ | $↗\\,\\,⌣$ | $\\text{max}$ | $↘\\,\\,⌣$ |\n\nNow, let's sketch our graph: \n\n- We draw a point on the vertical line $x=1$, where the derivative is undefined.\n\n- Since $x=1$ is a local maximum, the graph must go down to the left and to the right of that point.\n\n- The graph must be concave up on $(-\\infty ,1)\\cup (1,\\infty ).$\n\n- Finally, we are told that the function is continuous.\n\nTherefore, a possible graph of $f$ could be as follows:\n\n![](images/8c/8c4aa28d2fe102609adcc6c9dbc9f7bd859b6feed443acc78694091fbec5241f.png)"} :step/id #uuid "d9f8ea5a-e8df-5134-9ff1-2678961d9abf" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186507558}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186507588 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186507423 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1b25006d-a3ff-547c-8191-394bcd29aa7d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/5a/5a6bf2e08467fa35db0c5cc828549682b8cd25444b67c719088a608fcd0d8147.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506727} {:answer/id #uuid "2052247e-0f87-508a-8e44-91fc147a584e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/68/6881d55a3a048d20ba8320b401a60dcc0a3909b963ce05c61ebd81926bbb8268.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506742} {:answer/id #uuid "821d3c41-1585-5c03-994c-28bd818fcd41" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/8f/8f36e65777bd4983f41498f4c85fa856102e1ac602d675d4437cbaebc06aed44.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506964} {:answer/id #uuid "dc9565d2-4f0f-5c85-992f-1e1206c178bf" 